# Vue Files Structure Rule

## Template First, Script Second, No Styles

When working with Vue files (.vue), follow this specific structure:

1. **Template section** must come first
2. **Script section** must come second  
3. **Style sections** should be removed entirely

### Example Structure

```vue
<template>
  <!-- Your HTML template content here -->
  <div>
    <h1>Component Title</h1>
  </div>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
// Your TypeScript/JavaScript logic here
</script>
```

### Rules

- ✅ Template tags must be placed above script tags
- ✅ Remove all `<style>` tags and their contents
- ✅ Maintain proper indentation and formatting
- ❌ Do not include any style sections
- ❌ Do not place script tags before template tags

This rule ensures consistent Vue file structure across the project and removes unnecessary styling in favor of external CSS or component libraries.# Vue Files Structure Rule

